# EXPRESS-011 manual requests.
# 1. Start the server: npm run dev:express:11  (starts with no notes)
# 2. Click "Send Request" above a request (VS Code extension "REST Client").
# Saving task11.ts restarts the server and deletes the notes.

@host = http://localhost:3000

### Alice creates a note; ownerId from the body is ignored (expect 201, ownerId "u-alice", title trimmed)
POST {{host}}/notes
Authorization: Bearer token-alice
Content-Type: application/json

{ "title": "  Shopping list  ", "body": "Milk", "ownerId": "u-bob" }

### Alice creates a team note (expect 201, visibility "team")
POST {{host}}/notes
Authorization: Bearer token-alice
Content-Type: application/json

{ "title": "Team plan", "body": "", "visibility": "team" }

### Alice's notes (expect 200, both notes)
GET {{host}}/notes
Authorization: Bearer token-alice

### Bob's notes (expect 200, empty data: Alice's notes are not his)
GET {{host}}/notes
Authorization: Bearer token-bob

### Empty title (expect 400)
POST {{host}}/notes
Authorization: Bearer token-alice
Content-Type: application/json

{ "title": "   ", "body": "x" }

### Invalid visibility (expect 400)
POST {{host}}/notes
Authorization: Bearer token-alice
Content-Type: application/json

{ "title": "Plan", "body": "x", "visibility": "public" }

### No token (expect 401, already handled by the starter)
GET {{host}}/notes
